  "caveats": [
    "The eight selected native case records, including the known failed heterogeneous case, exactly equal the retained 16-case CPU report. This audit does not replace that broader report.",
    "The original 10x heterogeneous 4 ms backward reaches its iteration budget; discrepancies remain 4.3506% for force/velocity and 17.4594% for volume-energy material sensitivity. These fail unchanged tolerances. Its separate 1 ms fixture passes.",
    "Swept contact rejects recording on a Warp Tape before stepping. No swept-contact backward or gradient is implemented.",
    "The dense NumPy reference backward oracle uses direct solves and finite-difference projection Jacobians. It checks converged algebraic branches, not iterative cap, clipping, divergence or zero-weight suppression behavior; focused guard tests and the compiled reference cover those behaviors.",
    "The native comparison label exact is a tolerance category. It does not turn Neo-Hookean reference material sensitivities, heterogeneous mean-weight adjoints, frozen-contact state derivatives or clipped outputs into exact derivatives of the forward simulation.",
    "This CPU run does not validate CUDA graph behavior. Earlier 187-test suites and older training performance reports are separate historical evidence."
  ],
